  "hypothesis": "H79-H1 (G79-THVC): Unmapped Quaternary geothermal conduit and relay faults in the Great Basin produce a coupled multi-physics signature combining (i) multi-scale detrended 1-m 3DEP LiDAR scarp steps where available and multi-scale TPI/slope breaks across the 24.99% Nevada LiDAR gap, (ii) basement-depth-steered Bouguer/isostatic gravity gradients and magnetic hydrothermal demagnetization + Smectite clay alteration lows, (iii) DOE GDR 1391 (DOI: 10.15121/1881483) 2-m shallow temperature probe positive residuals, Quaternary sinter/travertine/tufa deposits, geothermometry spring clusters, and volcanic vent conduits, and (iv) fold-fair Mode-II/III crack-tip stress propagation lobes ahead of visible fault terminations.",
  "mechanism": "Two-stage nested spatial ensemble estimates exact-pixel and 300-m kernel-credit surrogate surfaces on 84 physical and visible-catalogue channels. A fixed-penalty lazy-greedy kernel-cover allocator uses lambda_fp=0.0022, min_sep_px=1.9 and a budget cap chosen on inner simulated data. The historical Charnes-Cooper name is an identifier, not a proof of exact fractional-programming optimality.",
  "named_non_fault_mimic": "Pleistocene pluvial paleo-shoreline wave-cut benches (Lake Lahontan and Lake Bonneville), fluvial terrace risers along the Humboldt/Carson/Walker rivers, welded ash-flow caldera cooling joints, and down-gradient lateral thermal outflow plumes in permeable alluvial fans.",
